  "name": "Chhayam (Khmer festival procession drumming)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Comic processional dance-music of Cambodia that leads ceremonial processions at the Khmer New Year in April and at Kathin, when gifts are carried to the monks at the end of the rainy season. Drummers on brightly decorated long drums (skor chhayam), with wooden krab clappers and hand cymbals, drive exaggerated clowning dances and raucous call-and-response singing that bystanders may join. A generic drum card stands in for the skor chhayam and an auxiliary-percussion card for the krab.",
